, or there; believe it not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤text¿Behold, I have told you before.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†Wherefore if they shall say unto you, Behold, he is in the desert; go not forth: behold, he is in the secret chambers; believe it not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKFor wheresoever the carcase is, there will the eagles be gathered together.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆImmediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊand then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse#¦verses”„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzNow learn a parable of the fig tree; When his branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is nigh:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\so likewise ye, when ye shall see all these things, know that it is near, even at the doors.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZVerily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass, till all these things be fulfilled.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCHeaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book'§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse,¦verses™„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZBut of that day and hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father only.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKBut as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšFor as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark,¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiand knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKThen shall two be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other left.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTTwo women shall be grinding at the mill; the one shall be taken, and the other left.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«But know this, that if the goodman of the house had known in what watch the thief would come, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken up.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVTherefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh.¦layout ªlast_verse,…¤book'§chapter«first_verse-ªlast_verse3¦verses—„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Who then is a faithful and wise servant, whom his lord hath made ruler over his household, to give them meat in due season?¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJBlessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGVerily I say unto you, That he shall make him ruler over all his goods.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQBut and if that evil servant shall say in his heart, My lord delayeth his coming;¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSand shall begin to smite his fellowservants, and to eat and drink with the drunken;¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqthe lord of that servant shall come in a day when he looketh not for him, and in an hour that he is not aware of,¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyand shall cut him asunder, and appoint him his portion with the hypocrites: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.¦layout ªlast_verse3